<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 29 December, from 1170 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1170 CE <span class="tih-ago">856 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Becket is murdered in Canterbury Cathedral</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four knights, believing they were carrying out Henry II's wishes, killed Archbishop Thomas Becket in his cathedral. Becket was canonised in 1173, and Canterbury became one of Europe's great pilgrimage sites.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/american-south" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-south.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1778 CE <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British forces capture Savannah</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A British expedition took Savannah, Georgia, opening a new campaign in the American South. The southern strategy brought early gains but ended with surrender at Yorktown in 1781.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1845 CE <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texas becomes the 28th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nine years after winning independence from Mexico, Texas was admitted to the Union as a slave state. The annexation helped provoke the Mexican-American War the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1890 CE <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops massacre Lakota at Wounded Knee</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">While disarming a band of Lakota at Wounded Knee Creek, South Dakota, the 7th Cavalry opened fire, killing some 250 to 300 men, women and children. It marked the end of the Plains wars.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Firebombs start the 'Second Great Fire of London'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German bombers dropped thousands of incendiaries on the City of London, starting some 1,500 fires. Much of the square mile burned, but St Paul's Cathedral survived amid the smoke.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
